FILE: app/src/pose-mode.ts
```ts
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { pauseAnimation, playAnimation } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function freezeForPosing(group: AnimationGroup): () => void {
    pauseAnimation(group);
    return () => {
        playAnimation(group);
    };
}
```

I created `src/pose-mode.ts` with `freezeForPosing` that calls `pauseAnimation` to stop the group from evaluating and writing to nodes each frame (so manual node edits persist), and returns a `resume` closure that calls `playAnimation` to continue from the preserved `currentTime` at the group's own `speedRatio`. I'm not sure of anything — the API declarations make the pause/play semantics clear.
